			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831432">
									

<p>Some questions and info that might help you see the issues here, and point you down a more productive path:</p>
<p>Why is it a millipede? Not just in the mechanical sense, but why, for the purposes of the story, is it a millipede rather than a centipede, or a robot, or a bowl of nachos with legs? There should be a why, at least in your mental notes. If there isn't: Why is it a millipede?</p>
<p>Why does it attack things? Again, if there isn't a reason: Why does it attack things?</p>
<p>Why is it a germaphobe? (This is actually the most interesting aspect at the moment, btw. Zero sarcasm: maybe give it cleaning supplies and have it join the site cleaning crew.)</p>
<p>What makes this an SCP? The Foundation has loads of giant bugs in containment. What makes this one require <em>Special</em> containment procedures instead of &quot;lock it up and feed it periodically&quot;</p>
<p>Potentially relevant info regarding millipedes: In the early days of land-dwelling life, millipedes were some of the largest creatures on Earth, some species measuring around 2 meters. They had no known predators. Almost all species of millipede (past and present) are herbivores. Their survival mechanisms are almost entirely defensive measures- they curl up, some taste bad or excrete mildly irritating chemicals, some have bristles&#8230;it's all protection, no offense. Some of the most harmless creatures on earth, really.</p>

